{"binary":"WGF11SharedResources.exe","reason":"Exhausted host GPU memory on the D3DMetal backend (suites/exclusions/d3dmetal.jsonl: Metal Insufficient Memory, kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory, and a host kernel panic on 2026-09-04).  That was D3DMetal's own allocations, and DXMT shares resources through different code, but the memory builds up across the binary's groups on the host GPU either way, so it is not run here to find out: a host GPU fault is a host-panic risk.","evidence":"WGF11SharedResources in the full sweeps of 2026-10-15 on Neptune and on CrossOver"}
{"binary":"WGF11Shader5x.exe","group":"Registers\\Limits\\Temp","reason":"Host GPU fault on DXMT: a render-server worker created at 18:55:55 had 12 Metal command buffers aborted with kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorInvalidResource right after 'object table: Create ... failed on the host', and the host's GPU-fault watchdog stopped the VM.  The group cannot be told apart from its neighbours (ConstantBuffers ended 18:54:30; the guest died with the VM before the fault group's per-case log was copied), so the three groups that started between 18:55:44 and 18:55:55 in the binary's order are kept out together; a host GPU fault is not re-run to narrow it.","evidence":"WGF11Shader5x in the Neptune DXMT full sweep of 2026-10-23: the render-server worker's aborted command buffers at 18:55:55 in the QEMU log, and the watchdog stopping the VM"}
